From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sheepsticked <72666364+Sheepsticked@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] uac: bound the playback write wait, drop frames, reopen the
 card

Upstream: https://github.com/IchthysMaranatha/asterisk-chan-quectel @ 3d45c7f072131296a7e3c1a4faf5bb18751dbd87
Purpose: with uac, the call's audio write sat in an unbounded retry while it
         held the device lock once the kernel's USB audio driver stopped
         draining the playback buffer, so the hangup was never handled, the
         CLI and AMI blocked and the call had no audio (applies on top of
         0014)

Upstream's channel_write() retries a playback write that answers -EAGAIN
(buffer full) every microsecond for as long as it takes, and a buffer that
stays full keeps the device lock for ever. The wait is now at most one
20 ms frame, in 1 ms steps, and none after a frame was dropped until a
write goes through again. A frame that does not fit is dropped (the write
still answers success, as for an XRUN) and counted. After 25 drops in a row
the sound card is closed and opened again, as for a playback stream that
never runs: emptying the buffer (snd_pcm_drop() and snd_pcm_prepare()) does
not get a stuck stream going, a reopened card does. While the buffer stays
full the card is reopened again every 250 further drops. The per-call line
gains "N frames dropped (playback full)".
---
 chan_quectel.h |  6 ++++++
 channel.c      | 58 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 2 files changed, 56 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chan_quectel.h b/chan_quectel.h
index 8fb47a0..366da84 100644
--- a/chan_quectel.h
+++ b/chan_quectel.h
@@ -29,6 +29,9 @@
 #include <alsa/asoundlib.h>
 #define PERIOD_FRAMES           80
 #define UAC_XRUN_STREAK_REOPEN  25	/* playback writes ending in XRUN, one after the other, before the card is reopened: 0.5 s of 20 ms frames */
+#define UAC_WRITE_WAIT_MS       20	/* longest wait for room in the playback buffer: one 20 ms frame */
+#define UAC_STALL_STREAK_REOPEN 25	/* playback frames dropped, one after the other, before the card is reopened: 0.5 s of 20 ms frames */
+#define UAC_STALL_REOPEN_RETRY  250	/* further dropped frames before the card is reopened again while the buffer stays full: 5 s */
 #define DESIRED_RATE 8000
 #define ALSA_PCM_NEW_HW_PARAMS_API
 #define ALSA_PCM_NEW_SW_PARAMS_API
@@ -152,6 +155,9 @@ typedef struct pvt
 	unsigned int		uac_underruns;			/*!< playback XRUNs of the current call */
 	unsigned int		uac_xrun_streak;		/*!< playback writes that ended in XRUN since the last one that did not */
 	unsigned int		uac_reopens;			/*!< sound card reopened during the current call (see channel_write()) */
+	unsigned int		uac_drops;			/*!< playback frames dropped in the current call because the buffer stayed full */
+	unsigned int		uac_stall_streak;		/*!< playback frames dropped since the last write that went through */
+	unsigned int		uac_stall_reopen_at;		/*!< stall streak at which the sound card is reopened next */
 	int			audio_fd;			/*!< audio descriptor */
 	int			data_fd;			/*!< data descriptor */
 	char			* alock;			/*!< name of lockfile for audio */
diff --git a/channel.c b/channel.c
index fc5268f..9d8c198 100644
--- a/channel.c
+++ b/channel.c
@@ -318,7 +318,7 @@ static void disactivate_call(struct cpvt* cpvt)
                 if (strcmp(CONF_UNIQ(pvt, quec_uac),"1") == 0) {
 			if (pvt->icard) snd_pcm_drop(pvt->icard);
 			/* the only trace of a starved or overflowing sound card: upstream logs an XRUN only in a DEBUG build */
